  "coverage": {
    "mode": "explicit-classified",
    "gaps": [
      "The command name in invoke(\"greet\") and the event name in listen(\"saved\") are string arguments; no JavaScript or TypeScript Pack publishes call arguments, so a CommandInvocation cannot be joined to the command it calls.",
      "#[tauri::command] arrives from omega-rust as reference.attribute named `command` spanning the attribute node alone, which is a sibling of the function it decorates and does not contain it, so no span join reaches the decorated function and the set of Tauri commands is not stated.",
      "omega-json, omega-json5 and omega-toml publish a config key's `value` as an attribute, which the overlay can only compare against a literal; window labels, capability identifiers and product names in the config files are therefore not carried as entity names.",
      "Plugin registration in Rust (.plugin(tauri_plugin_fs::init())) names the plugin in the path segment tauri_plugin_fs, which omega-rust does not emit; the plugin set is read from Cargo.toml and tauri.conf.json instead.",
      "Platform override merging, generated bindings, runtime windows and webviews, and command execution are runtime semantics no static fact states."
    ]
  },
